Focus the notification sender window after its default action is invoked.

Notification popups only call NotificationService.focusSenderWindow() when a
notification has no default action. Nearly every application sets one, and on
niri invoking it typically raises the window without switching to its
workspace, so clicking a notification appears to do nothing. Schedule a
compositor-side focus of the sender application instead, after giving the
application a chance to focus a specific window itself.

